  "blocks": {
    "\"Grill it first — make it ask you about partial cancels, refunds, and timing before it commits anything to the doc. Cheaper to resolve in conversation than in code.\"": "“先让它进行深度追问——在把任何内容写进文档前，让它询问部分取消、退款和时序。通过对话解决问题，比写进代码后再返工便宜。”",
    "\"It went straight to writing the spec and got the cancellation logic wrong.\"": "“它直接开始写规格说明，把取消逻辑做错了。”",
    "A technique for developing a design concept with an agent: the agent interviews the user Socratically, one decision at a time, proposing a recommended answer for each. Slows the rush to a finished plan — no handoff artifact is written until the concept stabilises.": "深度追问是一种与<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>共同发展设计概念的技术：智能体以苏格拉底式方式访谈用户，一次只处理一个决策，并为每个决策提出推荐答案。它会放慢急于完成计划的节奏——只有设计概念稳定下来后，才会写入<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/handoff-artifact\">交接产物</a>。",
    "It's a human-in-the-loop technique: your answers are the input. When a question can't be answered in conversation — you'd have to see the thing — switch to prototyping.": "这是一种人工介入技术：你的回答就是输入。当某个问题无法通过对话回答——你必须亲眼看到产物——就切换到<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/prototyping\">原型设计</a>。",
    "The technique exists because agents fill gaps silently. Asked to write a spec from a two-line prompt, the agent doesn't stop at the decisions you haven't made — it picks defaults and writes them in. The result looks complete, and the guesses are indistinguishable from the choices, so you discover them late: at review, or when the built feature handles an edge case in a way you never chose. Grilling inverts this — instead of guessing, the agent has to ask.": "这项技术之所以存在，是因为智能体会默默填补空白。当你让它根据两行提示词编写<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/spec\">规格说明</a>时，它不会停在尚未作出的决策前，而是自行选择默认值并写进去。结果看似完整，猜测与真正选择难以区分，于是你往往很晚才发现——可能是在审查时，也可能是在已构建功能处理某个你从未选择的边界情况时。深度追问将这一过程反转：智能体不再猜，而是必须提问。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
